config ENABLE_SNTP
	bool "Enable SNTP"
	default n
	help
	  Synchronizes the clock of the system using NTP server.(Requires internet connection)
	  Disabling means that the timestamps will start from boot up time.

config SNTP_SERVER_ADDRESS
	string "SNTP server address (host[:port])"
	depends on ENABLE_SNTP
	default "time.nist.gov"
	help
	  Server passed to Zephyr's sntp_simple(). On an isolated tap/demo
	  network, point it at the tap host (e.g. "192.168.10.1:12123") and
	  run an SNTP responder there — without a wall-clock epoch the
	  island stamps commands from 1970 and Autoware's vehicle_cmd_gate
	  rejects them as stale, so autonomous mode never actuates.

config ASI_SNTP_RESYNC_INTERVAL_S
	int "Seconds between SNTP re-syncs (0 disables)"
	depends on ENABLE_SNTP
	default 10
	help
	  A one-shot boot epoch is unbounded-error: whatever advances the
	  clock afterwards is never exactly real time, and every control
	  command the island stamps inherits the error. On the FVP the model
	  fast-forwards an idle guest, measured at ~10.5x real, so the offset
	  grows without limit; on silicon this is ppm-level and the interval
	  barely matters. The re-sync thread sleeps in KERNEL time, so a
	  racing guest clock re-syncs more often in real time. Set 0 to keep
	  the old one-shot behaviour.

config DDS_DOMAIN_ID
	int "Domain ID for CycloneDDS"
	default 2
	help
		This config sets the domain ID for CycloneDDS.

config DDS_NETWORK_INTERFACE
	string "Name of the network interface to be used by CycloneDDS"
	default ""
	help
	  When left undefined, CycloneDDS will automatically select an interface
	  based on its own criteria.

config LOG_LEVEL
	int "Log level for actuation module"
	default 1
	range 0 2
	help
	  This config sets the log level for actuation module.
	  0: No logs
	  1: Fatal, Error, Warning, Config
	  2: Debug
	  It is used to limit the rate of messages being published to the console.

